      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A superb turnkey apartment on the fourth floor of one of the most soughtafter developments in Dublin 1, this dualaspect home combines immaculate presentation with exceptional convenience.\r\n\r\nFinished in mint condition and tastefully decorated throughout, the property offers a bright, welcoming living space with excellent flow and a clever utility area neatly tucked off the hallway. Both eastfacing double bedrooms enjoy morning light, with the primary bedroom featuring a stylish ensuite, complemented by a large family bathroom finished to a high standard.\r\n\r\nResidents benefit from secure underground parking and a professional concierge service, enhancing comfort, security and daytoday ease.\r\n\r\nA standout opportunity to secure a pristine, dualaspect apartment in a premier Dublin 1 address.\r\n\r\nSpencer Dock is ideally located beside the IFSC and Convention Centre in the Dublin Dockland area. The apartment is surrounded by an array of cafes, restaurants, The Odeon Cinema, and local shops, along with many of the major firms in the finance and tech industry such as Citibank, Morgan Stanley, KPMG, PWC and over the coming year, Salesforce. East Point Business Park is a short walk away and across the River Liffey is the ever-popular Grand Canal Dock where many international companies like Facebook, Accenture and Google have set up their European Headquarters. \r\n\r\nThis is a very exciting time for the area with many new additional hotels and restaurants in development. \r\n\r\nThe LUAS red line (Point Village) is right on your doorstep; the area is also serviced by several Dublin Bus routes in short walking distance (less than 5 minutes); and is easy walking distance from Connolly Station and Busaras. The airport journey time is approx. 15 minutes and both the Aircoach and the 747 buses stop less than a 4 minute walk from the apartment. The Port tunnel is a 3 minute drive away with access to both the M50 and M1."
      },
